        <ExplanationTxt>SCHEDULE A, PART II, LINE 17A. PUBLIC CHARITY FACTS AND CIRCUMSTANCES (IRS REGULATION SECTION 1-170-9(F)(3).THE ORGANIZATION HAS A GOVERNING BODY OF 5 BOARD OF DIRECTOR MEMBERS WHICH FOR MANY YEARS HAS MAINTAINED A CONTINUOUS AND BODA FIDE PROGRAM WHICH SOLICITS MEMBERSHIP FEES (XXX MEMBERS IN 2022) AND HAS MONTHLY MEMBER LUNCHEON MEETINGS AND CONDUCTS ANNUAL FUND RAISING EVENTS TO RAISE FUNDS FROM INDIVIDUALS IN ORDER TO PROMOTE ENGINEERING EXPERTISE AND CAREERS IN INDIVIDUALS, THE UNIFORMED SERVICES AND PRIVATE INDUSTRY.THE ORGANIZATION IS A MEMBERSHIP ORGANIZATION WITH FIXED MEMBERSHIP RATES SET TO ENROLL A LARGE CROSS SECTION OF MEMBERS FROM THE PRIVATE, PUBLIC AND THE UNIFORMED SERVICES WITH LOW COST MEMEBERSHIP AND MONTHLY LUNCHEON FEES.THE ORGANIZATION MEETINGS AND ACTIVITIES ARE DESIGNED TO APPEAL TO MEMBERS WITH A BROAD COMMON INTEREST IN ENGINEERING.THE ORGANIZATION FOR MANY YEARS HAS GRANTED SCHOLARSHIPS TO STUDENTS INTERESTED IN ENGINEERING,SUPPORTED LOCAL STUDENT ACTIVITIES IN ENGINEERING AND MADE CHARITABLE CONTRIBUTIONS TO OTHER TAX EXEMPT PUBLIC INTEREST ORGANIZATIONS IN THE HUNDREDS OF THOUSAND OF DOLLARS.</ExplanationTxt>
